    {
      "id": "f7",
      "statement": "What distinguishes the alerts: both have 6 senders and 6 transfers, so they look alike at the indicator level. The recorded relationships differ. (a) Amounts: A-9278 received varied amounts totalling 357,000; A-9895 received six identical 2,500 amounts totalling 15,000. (b) Onward coverage: every A-9278 contributing transfer has an onward link, but only 3 of 6 for A-9895. (c) Depth: A-9278's paths run 3 links through two intermediate accounts to A-4989, in two separate sequences; A-9895's paths stop after 1 link at A-1415. (d) Devices: A-9278's path accounts A-9278, A-5092 and A-2897 all sent from the same device D-568, while no device is shared on A-9895's paths. (e) Timing: on the A-9278 paths, the gaps between the onward transfers themselves are 140,000–195,000 ms. None of the downstream path accounts (A-5092, A-2897, A-4989, A-1415) has a fan-in alert.",
