  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "id": "h1",
      "statement": "The A-9278 alert may reflect a coordinated pattern: several inbound credits, followed within minutes by repeated 3-step sequences of debits all sent from the single device D-568, with each step slightly smaller (138,000→135,000→132,000; 210,000→206,000→202,000). This is consistent with, but does not establish, one operator controlling A-9278, A-5092 and A-2897. The onward links record timing only; they do not show that the same funds moved, and a shared device does not show shared ownership or identity.",
      "references": [
        "s1",
        "r1",
        "p1",
        "p4",
        "e7",
        "e8",
        "e9",
        "e10",
        "e11",
        "e12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "h2",
      "statement": "The A-9895 alert may be a more benign collection pattern, for example six people each paying an identical 2,500 contribution, followed by one later debit. Only half the credits have an onward link, there is a single shallow link and no device is shared, so the indicator alone is weak. This interpretation is not established by the data.",
      "references": [
        "i2",
        "r2",
        "a1",
        "a2",
        "a3",
        "a4",
        "e19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "h3",
      "statement": "In arithmetic, T0007 (138,000) is close to the sum of T0002+T0003+T0006 (141,500), and T0014 (210,000) is close to T0010+T0011+T0012 (215,500). This could suggest aggregation at A-9278, but the dataset records only timing links, not the movement of funds.",
      "references": [
        "e1",
        "e2",
        "e3",
        "e4",
        "e5",
        "e6",
        "e7",
        "e10"
      ]
    }
  ],
